# Vectorization, said twice.  The top three lines are the explicit M-JELLY forms:
# ⊞ zip = elementwise binary op over two lists (′atom is auto-wrapped, so builtin
# ops pass straight to higher-order words), and broadcast built by hand out of a
# variable and a closure word.  The bottom three are the same three programs
# after M-VEC, where the bare + - * ⌈ ⌊ dispatch on shape themselves — pairs of
# lists zip, a list and an int broadcast, two ints stay plain arithmetic.
# Both halves print the same three lines; the second half is the shorter one, and
# neither is going away — ⊞ is still how any OTHER binary function meets a pair
# of lists, since only those five operators carry a shape hook.
5⍳5⍳′+⊞⍕␤            # elementwise sum of two range(5)s -> 0 2 4 6 8
4⍳4⍳′*⊞∑Ṅ␤           # dot product  range(4)·range(4)   -> 14
10→k:f←k+;5⍳′f€⍕␤    # broadcast +10 over range(5)      -> 10 11 12 13 14
5⍳5⍳+⍕␤              # the same, with the operator doing the looping
4⍳4⍳*∑Ṅ␤             #   list * list -> elementwise, then ∑
5⍳10+⍕␤              #   list + int  -> broadcast, no closure needed
